{"name":"Hearthstone","hex":"#c7beb2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hearthstone","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat stone used to form a hearth.","The fireside, home life."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To scour, as a floor, with hearthstone."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hearthstone"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hearthstone","blocks":[{"text":"Hearthstone is a 2014 free-to-play digital collectible card video game produced by Blizzard Entertainment. Originally subtitled Heroes of Warcraft, Hearthstone builds upon the existing lore of the Warcraft series by using the same elements, characters, and relics. The game is available on the Windows, macOS, iOS and Android platforms, featuring cross-platform play. It has been a critical and commercial success, with Blizzard reporting more than 100 million Hearthstone players as of November 2018, and the game has become popular as an esport, with cash prize tournaments hosted by Blizzard and other organizers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f2/Hearthstone_2016_logo.png/330px-Hearthstone_2016_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hearthstone","wikidata":"Q8262784"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/51/Hearthstone_screenshot.png/330px-Hearthstone_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/51/Hearthstone_screenshot.png/330px-Hearthstone_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An example of gameplay in Hearthstone. Players use cards from their hands, such as minions and spells, to interact with the game board.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHearthstone_screenshot.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/35/Hearthstone_screenshot_2.png/33